  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Find $\\text{Im}(k)$ given that \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\overset{\u2015}{kv}=[\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $\\overset{\u2015}{kv}=\\overset{\u2015}{k}\\,\\overset{\u2015}{v},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{kv} & =\\overset{\u2015}{k}\\,\\overset{\u2015}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{\u2015}{k}\\,\\overset{\u2015}{[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{\u2015}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{\u2015}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}\\,\\overset{\u2015}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n2\\text{i}\\,\\overset{\u2015}{k}=-6+8\\text{i}\\,\u27f9\\,\\overset{\u2015}{k}=\\frac{-6+8\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}=4+3\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{\u2015}{4+3\\text{i}}=4-3\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Im}(k)=-3.$",
